;
; DEED clause profile: NEUROSYM.deed, v1.0.0 (DRAFT)
; Prose and rationale: docs/estate-reconciliation/A7-contractiles-descriptiles-anchor.adoc
; sections 7.1 and 7.2 (the NEUROSYM.deed row); rulings J14, J20 and J35 to
; J37 of 2026-11-15 (the chora's (neurosym …) moves here whole; its A2ML
; @profile marker does not translate; (neural-config) holds no member until
; one is ruled). Field source: the ruled table of
; 1-formats/deed/mappings/agentic-neurosym-playbook-to-repo-deed.adoc
; (NEUROSYM.a2ml), applied in standards_chora.deed. M3 module order: section 11.
;
; A CLAUSE PROFILE, not a new grammar. Every rule below is also a `field` or
; `clause` of deed.abnf v2.0.0, so NEUROSYM.deed still passes deed_lint
; unchanged. Rules it borrows: string, symbol, boolean and token-sep are
; deed.abnf's; date-string and str-list1 are common.abnf's. Requires RFC 7405
; (%s"..." case-sensitive literals).
;
; Where it applies: NEUROSYM.deed (head descriptile-deed, J14), at the top
; level of the form. (hypatia …) is required; every other member is optional.
; SEMANTIC (validator-enforced, deed_lint.js --neurosym):
;   * the descriptile header, as for every descriptile (J20, J28, J4, YD06);
;   * each neurosym-field at most once, and at most one of each clause;
;   * no (rule …) (YF02), and no rule definition anywhere (YD05);
;   * with the chora deed read alongside, a chora (neurosym …) is warned, and
;     refused in strict mode (J35, YF06).

neurosym-field  = ( %s":version"      token-sep string )
                / ( %s":last-updated" token-sep date-string )
                / ( %s":rulesets"     token-sep str-list1 )
                ; :version and :last-updated come from the chora's
                ; (neurosym …) (J35). :rulesets selects rules from the A5
                ; registry: each entry is an A5 rule domain (A5 3.1, `domain`,
                ; such as "hypatia" or "rsr"), never a rule definition (YD05).
                ; SEMANTIC: the strings are not empty, and each :rulesets
                ; entry matches the A5 domain form, once.

ns-hypatia      = "(" %s"hypatia" 1*(token-sep hypatia-member) [token-sep] ")"
hypatia-member  = ( %s":scan-enabled"  token-sep boolean )
                / ( %s":scan-depth"    token-sep scan-depth )
                / ( %s":report-format" token-sep string )
scan-depth      = %s"quick" / %s"standard" / %s"deep"
                ; The mapping's ruled row: [hypatia-config] becomes
                ; (hypatia …), and scan-depth is a SYMBOL from a closed set
                ; of three. SEMANTIC: all three members, each exactly once.

ns-neural       = "(" %s"neural-config" ")"
                ; J37: no member is defined until one is ruled, so the clause
                ; is empty or absent. A populated [neural-config] fails closed
                ; in the mapping too.

ns-symbolic     = "(" %s"symbolic-rules" ")"
                ; YD05: rules live in the A5 registry, which :rulesets selects
                ; from; this clause holds no rule definition, so it is empty
                ; or absent.
